<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="JAS" style="id">- Onobasulu (ONN) - Onobasulu Translation Team - January 2007</book>
  <para style="h">Yemese</para>
  <para style="toc1">Yemese Sowi Ewe Seleba Ufulu</para>
  <para style="toc2">Yemese</para>
  <para style="toc3">Yem</para>
  <para style="mt">Yemese</para>
  <para style="mt2">Yemesehe Sowi Ewe Seleba Ufulu</para>
  <para style="imt">Sulu samini alegaeyo</para>
  <para style="ip">Yemese sowida selelu ewemo, Yesune elewobileba, dawalolo inolo auba solu.</para>
  <para style="ip">Yemesene sowi selelu ewehe sulu nafulu wedinale selelu dobu amomo. Godene idele inolomo mana nafulusu kuliba malesine selelu dobu.</para>
  <para style="ip">Idele inolo sagoba ufiyone, ehe besi sulu wedinale selelu. Ilihe asigi nafulu disia, ene sulu amo nafuluba asigimesine seleba dobu.</para>
  <para style="ip">Yemesehe kiwigaaba eweguba selefe. Inolo Yesufea asigi ule ufulu labe amo, balu miliyobafale koleba. Aubale. Ehe noolofea mana nafulu molofe amo walesiamo, e asigi ule ufulumo kiwida loluba walelo.</para>
  <para style="ip">
    <figure style="fig" alt="Separator Artwork for the Onobasulu NT - Waves" file="Separator1Onobasulu.tiff" size="span" loc="Between Book entry and text of the NT" copy="Johann Alberts, based on Onobasulu artwork" ref="1.0" /></para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JAS 1" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 1:1" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">1.1 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 13:55">Mad 13.55</ref>; <ref loc="GAL 1:19">Gal 1.19</ref>; <ref loc="ACT 15:13">HD 15.13</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 1:1">1Fid 1.1</ref></char>
    </note>Na <char style="w" lemma="Yemese[[3]], Yemese Bugoda selelumo, amo e">Yemese</char>. Godedai, <char style="w">Saminilo</char> Yesu <char style="w" lemma="Keliso">Kelisodaine</char> <char style="w" lemma="Balu dabalu moloba ofolo faibe">balu dabalu moloba ofolo</char> uleno, na lolu. Nahe,</para>
  <para style="b" vid="JAS 1:1" />
  <para style="p" vid="JAS 1:1">Sowi ewe, mosomu huguluba helefealu aleba budiba dedaleba yaalu alebaibumofea seleba mebaisu. Yudane sigidubulu idele inolo, na gilifea henelu sulu seleba mebaisu ewe.<verse eid="JAS 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="s">Dedeba bebelefe amohe nini kiwigaaba ofolo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 1:2" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">1.2 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="ROM 5:3-5">Lom 5.3-5</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, dedeba bebeleyo nokene nokeneba gili labea goasimo, gili koleba, amo heneyone kegelebuba hilisemale. <verse eid="JAS 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 1:3" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1.3 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="1PE 1:7">1Fid 1.7</ref></char></note>Mau enebamo, gili asigibu, gine <char style="w">asigi ule ufulu</char> ogofea dedeba besabimo, amohe gine miliyolu usu kiwi sanefia afelesiale, daabasu melesine mana moloba ofolaba ado. <verse eid="JAS 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 1:4" />Mana amohe gilifea dabalu moloba samodosihe, gilifea koleba kiwigaaba ufiyobafe. Auba molosihe, gili isoba fadaba moloba samodolu ligia, mana nafulufealomo, gilimo kegele ulenoda aboboyobafale.<verse eid="JAS 1:4" /></para>
  <para style="s">Inolo dawalolo nafulu diyo abobosenaga, amo e Godedai sulu saeyo dobu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 1:5" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">1.5 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="PRO 2:3-6">Snd 2.3-6</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Auluso, inolo uleno gili aleba ugi, dawalolo abobosenaga, amo gahe Godefea asigi memaba haalimale. Godehe kegele wedinale inolo suniafea gadibale besigaba melo. <verse eid="JAS 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 1:6" />Auluso, Godefea haalisiamo, ga koleba, asigi dabagalaba ligiale, <char style="w" lemma="Asigi ule ufulu">asigi ule ufia</char> melale. Mau enebamo, asigida dabagalafe e-mo, salu hano fufulo fuusi, fufuleba yaalo amogulu labe.<figure style="fig" alt="Who doubts is like the waves when the wind blows over the salt water" file="Gen01-04.jpg" size="col" loc="1.6" copy="Carolyn van Dyck" ref="1.6-8">Asigida dabagalafe e-mo, salu hano fufulo fuusi, fufuleba yaalo amogulu labe.</figure> <verse eid="JAS 1:6" /><verse number="7-8" style="v" sid="JAS 1:7-8" />Inolo asigi aida ligia, mana bubulilu amogulu molofe gahe, Saminilofea kegele uleno diyobasuba hilisemabiyo.<verse eid="JAS 1:7-8" /></para>
  <para style="s">Yemesehe weagulu inolo ilifeada, elebeda dobu inolo ilifeada, sulu saaba mefe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 1:9" />Nelewodali, nanodali, gili aleba ami wida male alebaibu gili amo, henemale. Mau enebamo, Godene si saabiamo, gilifeamo dabalu fogo ana melu dobu. <verse eid="JAS 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 1:10" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1.10 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ISA 40:6-7">Ais 40.6-7</ref></char></note>Auluso, inolo elebeda wedinale dobu gili amo, Godehe gine wi ana ogoda, gine dabalu fogo ana sebu ogoda, sisa ofa ilogosenaga, gili henemale. Maumo, elebeda ufulu ilimo, aale maamo odonologuba, odonoyobafe. <verse eid="JAS 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 1:11" />Halo holobagafia, koleba neeba dowesi, i bausosia, maamo odonofasia dulubaisiamo, ene yogolelu sunia asigileba yaalo. Amogubasu, elebeda inolo ene dabalu mololabia daabasu labi, odonoyobafe.<verse eid="JAS 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="s">Godehe ninifea nafulu moloba ofelesia, Ehe nini wolu molomesi sigiba dibia anale</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 1:12" />Dedeba babiyo holobagasihe, inolo kiwi sanefia afelesiale, daabasu adesenaga, amo e heneyo dobu. Enebamo, dedeba besabi, e kiwigaafia yoba alolune, elebe diyobafe. Elebe amo, Godehe Efeada hamesefe ili amofea meyoba saaba dobu. <verse eid="JAS 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 1:13" />Dedeba besabimo, “Godehe na wolu molomesi dedeba besabeba” samabiyo. Aubale. Enebamo, asigi woluhe Gode sigilale. Aufia, Gode Ehe, inolo wolu molomesi sigilale. <verse eid="JAS 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 1:14" />Aubale. Hilia sunia, inolo efea dedeba besabemo, ene mesegelo wolu amohe, e wolu molomesi hahanoba ofelesi sigilo. <verse eid="JAS 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 1:15" />Mesegelo <char style="w" lemma="Wolu / Wolu mololo">wolu</char> amohe, idohe faibe aseloguba asefasia, mana wolu seba dilo. Mana wolu amo buleba difasia, amohe olalo seba dilo.<verse eid="JAS 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 1:16" />Ne yagusodali koleba, gine asigi daaba dafolosi, nafuluba melale. <verse eid="JAS 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 1:17" />Kegele nafulu ninifea melu amoda, ulu dilo kegele yogolelu amoda, sunia hebenefia ano. Anakiwine yane suniada mololumo Ehe, kegele nafulu amo ninifea melo. Nine Nao amo, Ene manamo dedegelo male alefasia, asigi nololone asubaneda Efea male. <verse eid="JAS 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 1:18" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1.18 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="JHN 1:13">Yon 1.13</ref></char></note>Ene hame alefasia, seale sodohe nini seba dulu. Amohe, ninimo, Ene mololu amone <char style="w">sebe olaibo</char> melesifia, moloba ufulu.<verse eid="JAS 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="s">Nini sulu dofasia, kuliba daaba moloyoba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 1:19" />Ne yagusodali koleba, gili sulu ewe nafuluba asigimale. Dubiyofealomo, alebale domale. Auluso, sulu saeyofealomo, alebale samabiyo. Aufia, kanoyofealo amoda, alebale kanomabiyo. <verse eid="JAS 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 1:20" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1.20 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ECC 7:9">Sav 7.9</ref></char></note>Mau enebamo, inolone kanolo amohe, Godene mana isolu dibia holobagalale. <verse eid="JAS 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 1:21" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1.21 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="COL 3:8">Kol 3.8</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 2:1">1Fid 2.1</ref></char></note>Aulugulu, mana nugumalu suniada, wolu noolo afolu aso dobu ogoda, gilihe saidafaliba yaamale. Aufia, gilihe onaba ligia, sulu Godehe gine <char style="w">asigine libo</char> geba dobu amone dimale. Sulu amohe, gili <char style="w" lemma="Gasiba dafelagoba dilo">gasiba dafelagoba diyobafe</char>.<verse eid="JAS 1:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 1:22" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">1.22 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 7:26">Mad 7.26</ref>; <ref loc="ROM 2:13">Lom 2.13</ref></char>
    </note>Godene sulu balu domabiyo. Aubale. Ene sulu dofasia, kuliba daaba molomale. Balu dobelesenaga, gili gine meleba gegefe. <verse eid="JAS 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 1:23" />Inolo uleno Godene sulu mana balu dofasia, kuliba daaba molosalenaga, amo e inolo ene mi hewo bologuba besabe. <verse eid="JAS 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 1:24" />Ene mi hewo bafasia, abia, alebale hamagi, ene misi halagulu abulubiba galilo. <verse eid="JAS 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 1:25" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1.25 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ROM 8:2">Lom 8.2</ref>; <ref loc="JAS 2:12">Yem 2.12</ref></char></note>Auluso, inolo Godene sulu <char style="w">muguli</char> nafuluba fadaba baafia, sulu amo kuliba aafemo, Godehe inolo amo e molofemo <char style="w" lemma="Edililo - Ediliba Ofolo">ediliba</char> ufiyobafe. Sulu muguli nafulu amohe, idele inolo sububa dafelagolo.<verse eid="JAS 1:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 1:26" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">1.26 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="PSA 141:3">Sng 141.3</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Inolo uleno hilisesia, “Na Godedai seale gulugululoba” hiliseba ligiaso, ene eane nafuluba luba adesalenaga, amo e, ene meleba gegeba labe. Aulune, ene gulugululo mana amo, eleda male koleba adefe. <verse eid="JAS 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JAS 1:27" />Gulugululo mana seale isolu Gode hamefemo, ewe. Ilisulu ilida, kuluba faibili ilida, ili higinilu sebumo sagoba ufiyo dobu. Aufia, kegele nomo ewe. Helefealune nuguma wolu amohe nini medelosi, ninihe nine meleba nafuluba luba miliyo dobu.<verse eid="JAS 1:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JAS 2" />
  <para style="s">Nini mana imini ulesu inolo suniafea moloyo dobu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 2:1" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2.1 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="ACT 10:34">HD 10.34</ref>; <ref loc="JAS 2:9">Yem 2.9</ref></char>
    </note>Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, doma. Gilihe nine <char style="w">Saminilo</char> <char style="w">elalelu,</char> Yesu <char style="w" lemma="Keliso">Kelisofea</char> <char style="w">asigi ule ufulu</char> waalebu. Aulune, gilihe ulenofeasu bisigia molomabiyo. Aubale. Idele inolo suniafea, imini ule aibasu molomale. <verse eid="JAS 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 2:2" />Dedeba selesu. Inolo uleno fagulo yogolelu kaafia, golo sisilu sone kaafia, gili gagaiyofea ami suga saabi, inolo weagulu fagulo bibidilu kaafia, eda suga saabimo, <verse eid="JAS 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 2:3" />gilihe fagulo yogolelu kaalu amo bisigia, efea selesia, “Ga molobu nafulu ewe mesaba” saafia, inolo weagulu amofea selesia, “Ga ugi degeba mela” me “Ne emo aniba helea yoba mesaba” selesenaga, <verse eid="JAS 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 2:4" />amo gili imini ule aiba molobebelefale. Ausenaga, gilihe gine asigi wolu amofea alefasia osolafe.<verse eid="JAS 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 2:5" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2.5 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="1CO 1:26-28">1Kld 1.26-28</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Ne yagusodali, gili doma. Helefealu inolo si saabia iwi weagulu alebaibu ili amo, Godehe ine asigi ule ufulufealomo, elebeda ufulu melesine molobebelelu labe. Aufia, ili koleba, Godehe Yasifia Luba Ligia Saminilo Ada amone daalo dimesine, molobebelelu alebaibu. Godehe Efeada hamesebu ili amosu daalo amo dimesiba saaba ufulu dobu. <verse eid="JAS 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 2:6" />Auluso, gilihe, inolo weagulu ili amo yuaba ufulubu. Hilisema. Abehe gili dufa dafogosia, higinilu diba ofelesia, gili fadaayone sigiba dibia aso? Elebeda ufulu ili amosu gilifea mana auba mololo. <verse eid="JAS 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 2:7" />Godehe Kelisone wi nafulumo gilifea diba dobu ogomo, abehe wi amofea gaidaboba sodo? Elebeda ufulu ili amosu auba sodo. Aulugulu, gilihe elebeda ufulu amofeasu bolomo, enesi ause?<verse eid="JAS 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 2:8" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2.8 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 19:19">Mad 19.19</ref>; <ref loc="GAL 5:14">Gal 5.14</ref></char>
    </note>Gode E nine Saminilo luba ado labe. Ene sulu <char style="w">muguli</char> ninifea molomafe. “<char style="qt">Gahe gene meleba hamesefegubasu koleba, no anogoda aubasu hamesemale.</char>” Gilihe sulu muguli amo kuliba aasenaga, gili mana nafulu moloba labe. <verse eid="JAS 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 2:9" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.9 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="DEU 1:17">Lo 1.17</ref></char></note>Auluso, gilihe ulenofeasu bisigia molosenaga, amo gili <char style="w" lemma="Wolu / Wolu mololo">wolu</char> moloba ligia, sulu muguli amo geleba labe. <verse eid="JAS 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 2:10" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.10 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="LEV 19:37">Wkp 19.37</ref>; <ref loc="NUM 20:7-12">Nam 20.7-12</ref>, <ref loc="NUM 20:24">24</ref>; <ref loc="MAT 5:19">Mad 5.19</ref></char></note>Aulugulu, gilihe muguli mana sunia kuliba abiaso, muguli mana ulenoda gelesenaga, amo gilihe muguli mana amo sunia gelefe. <verse eid="JAS 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 2:11" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.11 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="EXO 20:13-14">Kis 20.13-14</ref>; <ref loc="ROM 13:9">Lom 13.9</ref></char></note>Nini asigibu. Godehe sulu muguli ofelesia, <char style="qt">susugu mana molomabiyolu</char>. Aufia, Ehe sulu muguli eweda ufulu. <char style="qt">Inolo dufa olamabiyo.</char> Aulugulu, ga-mo, susugu mana molosiale, inolo uleno dufa olasenaga, amo ga sulu muguli gelelo adefe.<verse eid="JAS 2:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 2:12" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2.12 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="GAL 6:2">Gal 6.2</ref>; <ref loc="JAS 1:25">Yem 1.25</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 2:16">1Fid 2.16</ref></char>
    </note>Aulune, muguli amohe, gili selefe amoda, gili molofe amoda, osolaeyobafebuba hilisefia, sulu saamale. Aufia, gili auba hilisefia, mana molomale. Sulu muguli amohe idele inolo sububa dafogolo. <verse eid="JAS 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 2:13" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.13 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="MAT 5:7">Mad 5.7</ref>; <ref loc="MAT 18:32-35">18.32-35</ref></char></note>Aulugulu, inolo ulenohe, inolo no anogofea kanululalenaga, amo Godehe e osolasia fadaafeiyamo, efeada kanuluyobafale. Auluso, <char style="w" lemma="Kanululo">kanululohe</char> osolalomo suniafia, wasolu dobu.<verse eid="JAS 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s">Asigi ule ufuluhe mana nafulu moloba dafelagosalenaga, amo weaselo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 2:14" />Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, doma. Inolo uleno selesia, “Na Kelisofea <char style="w">asigi ule ufulu</char> loluba” selaba ligiaso, e mana nafuluda moloba dafelagosalenaga, inolo amone asigi ule ufulu amo weasefe koleba. Asigi ule ufulu mana amogulu amohe, e obegeba diyodolula? Diyodoluale koleba. <verse eid="JAS 2:14" /><verse number="15-16" style="v" sid="JAS 2:15-16" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.15-16 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="1JN 3:17">1Yon 3.17</ref></char></note>Auba hilisema. Ge damene uleno, faguloda, naiyoda, male labimo, ga efea ene domala sagoba ufiyone kegele mebale ligia, selesia, “Fagulo domala halomesi kaafia, naiyo kubalemesi nafasia, <char style="w" lemma="Aealo - Aeaba Ofolo">aeafia</char> malaleba” selesenaga, ge sulu balu solu amohe, e sagoba ufiyobafela? Sagoba ufiyobafale. <verse eid="JAS 2:15-16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 2:17" />Amogubasu, asigi ule ufulu balusu ligia, mana nafulu moloba dafelagosalenaga, amoda, olalu dobu.<verse eid="JAS 2:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 2:18" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2.18 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="GAL 5:6">Gal 5.6</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Auluso, inolo ulenohe eweguba saeyobafe. “Ulenomo, asigi ule ufulu dobu. Nomo, mana nafulu mololo.” Inolo amo auba selesi, na efea eweguba obegeba saeyobasu. “Inolo uleno mana nafulu moloba dafelagosalenaga, amo nahe ene asigi ule ufulu ogo, eneba eloba babiyobi?” Auluso, mana nafulu molofe amofea alefasia, ne asigi ule ufulu mana amone, gafea eloba bamesine waleyobasu. <verse eid="JAS 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 2:19" />Gahe Gode ule E-su labeba <char style="w" lemma="Asigi ule ufulu">asigi ule dobula</char>? Amo nafulu. Auluso, <char style="w">gamodo</char> ilida, aubasu asigi ule ufia ligia, ili Gode baaba wobasubale sagilisia bibililo.<verse eid="JAS 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 2:20" />Ga asigidale inolo. Ga aso fadaba asigibualela? Asigi ule ufulumo mana nafuluda mololalemo weaseloba, na gafea saabia fadaba waleba saeyobile? <verse eid="JAS 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 2:21" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.21 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="GEN 22:9-12">Stt 22.9-12</ref></char></note>Saminimo, nine nauwa <char style="w">Abalahama</char> ehe, ene faibe Aisegemo <char style="w" lemma="Soba meyone defene olabolu">soba meyone</char>, defene olaboiya ofelesia, Godefea ulu melu. Ausi, fogo amo, Godehe ene mana amone bisigia, <char style="w" lemma="Godedai isoba melesi moloba ofolo">e isolu inoloba solu</char>. <verse eid="JAS 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 2:22" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.22 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="HEB 11:17-18">Hib 11.17-18</ref></char></note>Ga nafuluba asigima. Abalahama ene asigi ule ufulu amodai, ene mana nafulu amodai, aine dafifia ligia, ene mana mololu amohe, ene asigi ule ufulumo liliba ufulu. <verse eid="JAS 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 2:23" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2.23 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="GEN 15:6">Stt 15.6</ref>; <ref loc="2CH 20:7">2Sto 20.7</ref>; <ref loc="ISA 41:8">Ais 41.8</ref></char></note>Godene bugohe eweguba selelu dobu. <char style="qt">Abalahamahe Godefea asigi ule ufulune, Godehe e isolu inoloba solu. </char>Aufia, Ehe Abalahamafea selesia, “Ga ne dameneba” solu. <verse eid="JAS 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 2:24" />Ausiane, gili bisigiamo, asigi ule ufulu amosuale, mana nafulu molofe amoda alefasia, Godehe inolo uleno amo e isolu inoloba sodo.<verse eid="JAS 2:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 2:25" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2.25 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="JOS 2:1-21">Jos 2.1-21</ref>; <ref loc="HEB 11:31">Hib 11.31</ref></char>
    </note>Amogubasu, susugu mololo ido <char style="w" lemma="Lahabo">Lahabohe</char> mana nafulu molosi, Godehe e-mo isolu idoba solu. Enebamo, e Isolaelene aibasilo inolo aalumo, heneba milaba wefasia, aine gisa ilihe aalu selosi, ehe aalufea eno nolobalo fisaba malalu.<verse eid="JAS 2:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 2:26" />Nini asigibu, domala asubaneda male labe amo, olalu dobu. Aubasu, asigi ule ufulu mana nafuluda male labe amoda, olalu dobu.<verse eid="JAS 2:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JAS 3" />
  <para style="s">Eane nafuluba fofoyoba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 3:1" />Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, doma. Gili aleba ugi, inolo wedinalehe Godene sulu mana walelo alebaiyo hamelosi. Mau enebamo, Godehe walelo ine mana osolasiamo, idele inolo noolo ine mana osolaloguba, osolaeyobafale. Aubale. Ehe walelo ilifeamo nokene koleba osolaeyobafe. <verse eid="JAS 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 3:2" />Nini sunia mana wedinalefealomoda gelebaisalo. Auluso, inolo ene sulu sodofealomoda gelebaisalenaga, amo e isolu inolo koleba. Enebamo, ehe ene domala sunia isoba malesi, luba miliyodolu labe.<verse eid="JAS 3:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 3:3" />Eweguba asigima. <char style="w" lemma="Dofene hoso">Dofene hosomo</char>, kelebulu bule labe. Auluso, e-mo nini hamefeguba malesine, ninihe ene mofemo aeyene gelelu haisimo diba ofolo. Aeyene amo sigisiamo, ninihe ene domala suniamo yasilo. <verse eid="JAS 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 3:4" />Aufia, dedeba sulu nomo ewe. Hano sibi amone mana amoda asigima. Sibi amo bule kegele. Fufulo kolelumohe sibimo salu hano saabia malesi mololo. Sibida isoba malesi, hanoda olabolo amo wedino kegele koleba. Auluso, selo inolohe nolobalo maiyo hilisesiamo, e olabolo amo noloba ofelesi, hano sibimo e hamefeguba ano. <figure style="fig" alt="Large ship" file="44_Ac_18_13_RG.jpg" size="col" copy="Sweet Publishing" ref="3.4">Hano sibi</figure> <verse eid="JAS 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 3:5" />Amogubasu, eanemo, e domalafea wedino kegele labeso, e bule koleba bamabamasia, eleliba ado. Nini hilisebu, de waiya wedinomo alefasia, ilo bule sunia dagiyodolu dobu. <verse eid="JAS 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 3:6" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">3.6 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="MAT 12:36-37">Mad 12.36-37</ref>; <ref loc="MAT 15:11">15.11</ref>, <ref loc="MAT 15:18-19">18-19</ref></char></note>Eane e-mo, de amogulu labe. Nine domala haisi haisiba aleba amimo, wedino kegele nomo, e. Auluso, amofea alefasia wolu kegele noolo holobagaba yaalo. Ehe domala sunia medesia, nugumaba ofelesia, mana wolu nokene nokeneba nine miliyolu aleba ami, de kolelu waiyaba ofolo. De amo, <char style="w" lemma="Heli">helifia</char> ano koleba.<verse eid="JAS 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7-8" style="v" sid="JAS 3:7-8" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">3.7-8 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="ROM 3:13">Lom 3.13</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Inolohe ilo hele kelebulu suniada, hano aselo kelebulu suniada, hagada, koanoda, hanida, fofoyodolu dobuso, inolone eane fofoyodoluale koleba. Eane amo luba miliyodoluale wolu kegele koleba, e soiye aiyane inoloda dufa olalo amogulu labe.<verse eid="JAS 3:7-8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 3:9" />Eane hamaga ule amo e-su alefasia, ninihe <char style="w">Saminilo</char> nine Naone wi digiba safasia, inolo Godene mimisililu mololu labe amofea kaoba sodo. <verse eid="JAS 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 3:10" />Henelu suluda, kaolu suluda, mofe ule hamagasu aalifaba holobagagaba sodo. Nelewodali, nanodali, doma. Ewe auba miliyodoluale dobu. <verse eid="JAS 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 3:11" />Hano sugulo ulenohe, hano galagololuda, hano kabiluda, aalifaba holobagalola? Auba holobagalale. <verse eid="JAS 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 3:12" />Nelewodali, nanodali, doma. <char style="w" lemma="Olono i - Olono sebe">Olono ihe</char>, <char style="w">olifi</char> sebe helelola? <char style="w">Waini</char> efolohe, <char style="w" lemma="Olono i - Olono sebe">olono sebe</char> helelola? Auba helelale. Amogubasu, hano sugulo ubailu wolu amohe, hano galagololu holobagalale.<verse eid="JAS 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="s">Inolo dawalolo nafulu dobu, ehe mana nafulu mololo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 3:13" />Gili aleba ugi, inolo asigi nafuluda, dawaloloda, labela? Inolo amogulu elenaga, e adefeamo, ene miliyolu isolu ligia, dawaloloda onafia ligia, mana nafulusu moloba waleyo dobu.<verse eid="JAS 3:13" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 3:14" />Auluso, babiyo haboloda, kabilu manada, asigume manada, gine libo ufia labenaga, amo ga koleba, “Na dawalolo inolo loluba” bamabamaba samabiyo. Gili auba selesenaga, seale sodomo dabagalaba selefe. <verse eid="JAS 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 3:15" />Enebamo, dawalolo amogulumo hebenefasia inigiale, helefealufia ano. Amo inolone asubanefeasu alefasia, enao henanefea dofelefia ano. <verse eid="JAS 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 3:16" />Enebamo, babiyo habolo manada, asigume manada, mana amogulu dobia ami, idele inolo belagusia, mana wolu nokene nokeneba moloba ado.<verse eid="JAS 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="li">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 3:17" />Auluso, dawalolo hebenefia ano amo, samini kolebamo, galagololu ano.</para>
  <para style="li" vid="JAS 3:17">Aufia, aeafia hameselo.</para>
  <para style="li" vid="JAS 3:17">Aufia, gadisiale onafia ado.</para>
  <para style="li" vid="JAS 3:17">Aufia, sulu solu sigiba dobolo.</para>
  <para style="li" vid="JAS 3:17">Aufia, <char style="w">kanululo</char> wasigafia sebe nafulusu helelo.</para>
  <para style="li" vid="JAS 3:17">Aufia, waseba gigidifia osolalale.</para>
  <para style="li" vid="JAS 3:17">Aufia, dawalolo amo, masega sodale.<verse eid="JAS 3:17" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 3:18" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">3.18 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 5:9">Mad 5.9</ref>; <ref loc="HEB 12:11">Hib 12.11</ref></char>
    </note>
    <char style="w" lemma="Aealo - Aeaba Ofolo">Aeaba</char> ofa mololo idele inolo ilimo, aealo amone edo fififia, isolu mana amone sebe nafulu sulo.<verse eid="JAS 3:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JAS 4" />
  <para style="s">Inolohe helefealu mana hamefe amo, e Godedai gisa labe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 4:1" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">4.1 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="ROM 7:23">Lom 7.23</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Gili aleba ugi, belaguba ligia, hegeba adese ogo, mau amene ause? Maumo, asigi degeba yaalo mana amo gilifea dobu. Amohe, gine domala aleba ugi belaguba adefe. Me aufalebile? <verse eid="JAS 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 4:2" />Gilihe kegele diyo hameloso, dilalebu. Gilihe kegele dibaiyeba mesegefia, no anogofea gogoloba besabi, kegele amo diyodoluale ado. Aulune, gili hegesia belagulo. Auluso, gili kegele difale, maumo, gili Godefea memasia haalilalebu. <verse eid="JAS 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 4:3" />Me, gili Godefea kegele haaliloso, heleba woba haalilone, amo gili dilale. Gene hamefeguba moloyone haalisi, dilalebu.<verse eid="JAS 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 4:4" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">4.4 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="ROM 8:7">Lom 8.7</ref>; <ref loc="1JN 2:15">1Yon 2.15</ref></char>
    </note>Gili Gode gadefia dedalelu ogomo, idohe ene aino gadefia, susugu moloyone anoguba, dedalelubu. Helefealune mana hamelo amohe, Godene gisa ado. Gili amo asigifalela? Aulugulu, inolo abehe, helefealune manadai damene adesenaga, amo e Godedai gisa adefe. <verse eid="JAS 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 4:5" />Godene bugomo eweguba selefe. Godehe nini molosia amimo, nine libo usu iwimo, asubane melesi gadefalu. Aulune, ainohe ene eamono susugu molomesiale hameloguba, amogubasu, Godehe nini Efea faiso memesialesia, ninimo, nine asubane Efeasu asigifia melesi hamefe. Sulu amo Godene Bugo usu balu selelu dobuba hilisemabiyo. <verse eid="JAS 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 4:6" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.6 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="PRO 3:34">Snd 3.34</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 5:5">1Fid 5.5</ref></char></note>Godehe nini bule koleba <char style="w">kanululo</char>. Aulune, Godene bugo selesia,</para>
  <para style="b" vid="JAS 4:6" />
  <para style="q" vid="JAS 4:6">
    <char style="qt">“Inolo ili ine meleba wi digifia bamabamafemo,</char></para>
  <para style="q" vid="JAS 4:6">
    <char style="qt">Godehe ili anosi kaaba dafolo labe.</char></para>
  <para style="q" vid="JAS 4:6">
    <char style="qt">Auluso, inolo ili ine meleba helea adefe amomo,</char></para>
  <para style="q" vid="JAS 4:6">
    <char style="qt">Ehe kanulufia, mana nafulu moloba ofolo.”</char><verse eid="JAS 4:6" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 4:7" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">4.7 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="EPH 6:12">Efe 6.12</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Aulugulu, gili Gode sisa melale. Aufia, gilihe <char style="w">henane</char> iluwasia, e anosi kaamale. Auba kaasi, e gili gadefia fisaba maiyobafe. <verse eid="JAS 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 4:8" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.8 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ZEC 1:3">Sek 1.3</ref>; <ref loc="MAL 3:7">Mal 3.7</ref>; <ref loc="ISA 1:16">Ais 1.16</ref></char></note>Gili kolebamo, Gode aniba daafia adesimo, Eda inigia, gili aniba miliyo miyobafe. Mana <char style="w" lemma="Wolu / Wolu mololo">woluda mololo</char> gili koleba, gine sone nuguma heemale. Aufia, asigi aidaba ado idele inolo, gili gine asigi sawaba damale. <verse eid="JAS 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 4:9" />Gine wolu moloba alolu amone hilisesia, yagunagafia, yegilisia kuanomale. Gine gaidefe mana ogo afasia, kuanoba yegilimale. Gine henelo mana ogo afasia, asigi higinimale. <verse eid="JAS 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 4:10" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.10 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="JOB 5:11">Jop 5.11</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 5:6">1Fid 5.6</ref></char></note>Gili gine meleba koleba, <char style="w" lemma="Saminilo">Saminilone</char> olegia helea melale. Gilihe auba molosenaga, Saminilohe gili digiba lagoyobafe.<verse eid="JAS 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="s">Gine meleba osolamabiyo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 4:11" />Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, doma. Gine geleba saaba duduba woba samabiyo. Inolo abehe, no anogofea saaba duduba woba selesia, osolafe amo, ehe sulu <char style="w" lemma="Muguli">mugulifea</char> woba selesia osolafe. Gilihe sulu muguli osolasenaga, amo gili sulu muguli amone sisa adale ligia, amone osolalo adefe. <verse eid="JAS 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 4:12" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.12 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ROM 2:1">Lom 2.1</ref>; <ref loc="ROM 14:4">14.4</ref></char></note>Muguli manamo, Gode ule E-su saaba ufulu. Aufia, idele inoloda fadaasia osolalomo, Gode ule E-su labe. Amo idele inolo obegeba diyoda, woba dafiyoda, amo E-su labe. Auluso, ga abeba hilisesia, ge damene no anogo osolase?<verse eid="JAS 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="s">Nini eleliyobale</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 4:13" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">4.13 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="LUK 12:18-20">Lug 12.18-20</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Gili abehe selesia, “Aga, me aide, nini dauno no anogo dafasia, hamu ule ami ligia, bisinese dabalu molosia, mole bule diyoba” sodo amo, gili doma. <verse eid="JAS 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 4:14" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.14 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="PRO 27:1">Snd 27.1</ref>; <ref loc="PSA 39:5">Sng 39.5</ref>, <ref loc="PSA 39:11">11</ref></char></note>Gilihe sulu amoguba sodo amo, gili aide amene holobagaeyobafeba hilisebuale. Gine miliyolu ogo halagulu? Kene hoo holobagafia, wedino alefasia asigilelo, gili amogulu labe. <verse eid="JAS 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 4:15" />Auluso, gili eweguba saamale. “Saminilone hamenaga, nini aso isigia, kegele ewe, me anogo moloyobasuba” saamale. <verse eid="JAS 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 4:16" />Auluso, aga gili amoguba saabale ligia, kegele auba moloyoba elelisia, bamabamaba adobu. Elelilo mana amogulumo wolu koleba. <verse eid="JAS 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 4:17" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.17 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="LUK 12:47">Lug 12.47</ref></char></note>Gilihe mana nafulu ewe moloyo dobuba hilisefia ligiaso, auba molosalenaga, amo gili <char style="w" lemma="Wolu / Wolu mololo">wolu</char> molofe.<verse eid="JAS 4:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="JAS 5" />
  <para style="s">Inolo elebeda ufulu ilifea haguguba solu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 5:1" />Idele inolo elebeda ufulu amo, gili doma. Higinilu bule gili labea holobagaeyobafe. Aulune, gili galagiliba yegilima. <verse eid="JAS 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 5:2" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.2 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="MAT 6:19">Mad 6.19</ref></char></note>Gine elebe belaba samodolu dobu. Aufia, gine fagulo bibiyu naba samodolu dobu. <verse eid="JAS 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 5:3" />Gine <char style="w" lemma="Golo">goloda</char>, silifada, ginalogalihe naba samodolu dobu. Ginalogali amohe, gine wolumo fadaasia, gilifea oloba koweba saeyobafe. Aufia, amohe gine domalamo de nologuba naiyobafe. Aleba eloyo hiliamo holobagaeyo hagoalesi, gilihe gine elebe balu gagaiyofia daunagalu dobu. <verse eid="JAS 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 5:4" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.4 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="DEU 24:14-15">Lo 24.14-15</ref></char></note>Nafuluba doma! Dabalu moloba ofolo faibili ilihe, gine geiya ugi sebe suba labi, gilihe ili gegesia, ine elebe sunia meluale. Mole haisi meluale amohe, wuaaba selaba ligia, gilifea oloba koweba selefe. Sebeda sulo ilifea gilihe elebe sunia melualene yegilifemo, <char style="w">Saminilo</char> Kiwigagalu amone koneni sugafe. <verse eid="JAS 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 5:5" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.5 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="LUK 16:25">Lug 16.25</ref></char></note>Hilia sunia gili helefealu iwi sigia, kegele nenafolosu diabasu labene, gine domala ogo heneba ofolabasu labe. Gili auba moloba ligia, dufelesia dasigaeyo hilia amone gagaluba ufulu dofene amogulu alebaibu. <verse eid="JAS 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 5:6" />Gilihe isolu inolo fadaafia dufa danesi, ili iluwaba yaaluale.<verse eid="JAS 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="s">Ninihe asigi kiwigaafia, higinilu diaba ligia, Saminilo milesi yasiyoba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 5:7" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">5.7 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="JER 5:24">Jer 5.24</ref>; <ref loc="DEU 11:14">Lo 11.14</ref></char>
    </note>Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, gili koleba, gine asigi kiwigaafia esebalo ligia, Saminilo milesi yasimale. Gili asigibu. Gelu enao e-mo, ene geiya ami ele nafulu helemesi yasilo. E asigi kiwigaafia esebalo ligia, kene gidai, heleso gidai, holobagamesi yasilo. Aufia dufiamo, ele amone dilo. <verse eid="JAS 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 5:8" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.8 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ROM 13:11-12">Lom 13.11-12</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 4:7">1Fid 4.7</ref></char></note>Saminilo obegeba miyo fogomo hagoale adefegulu, gilida asigi kiwigaafia esebalo ligia, gine libo ogo bubulibale melale. <verse eid="JAS 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 5:9" />Nelewodali, nanodali, gili fadaasia osolalosine, gine geleba gogomoba samabiyo. Bama. Osolalo Inolomo eno saliba yoba labe.<verse eid="JAS 5:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 5:10" />Ne yagusodali, gili higinilu diaba ligia, asigi kiwigaafia, hamedofa miliyone mana amo halaguba alolubiba asigiyo hilisesenaga, amo <char style="w">saaba ofolo</char> samini alebailu amone asigimale. <verse eid="JAS 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 5:11" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.11 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="EXO 34:6">Kis 34.6</ref>; <ref loc="JOB 1:21-22">Jop 1.21-22</ref>; <ref loc="JOB 2:10">2.10</ref>; <ref loc="PSA 103:8">Sng 103.8</ref></char></note>Doma. Inolo ili amo kiwi sanefia afelesiale dedalebasu alolumo, ine henelo wasigafia alebailu. Ninihe ili amone saaba auba sodo. Inolo Yoba amo, ehe kiwi sanefia afelesiale daabasu aloluba solumo, gili dubulu. Aufia, mana Saminilohe efea dufia mololumo, gili abulu. Saminilo Ehe nini bule yagunagafia ligia, hilia sunia E nini kanulufia labe.<verse eid="JAS 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="s">Aiiba samabiyo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 5:12" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">5.12 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 5:34-37">Mad 5.34-37</ref>
      </char>
    </note>Ne nelewodali, kegele olaibo koleba, gili moloyo dobumo, ewe. Gili <char style="w">hebene</char> wi saabada, helefealu kegele noolo amone wi saabada, <char style="w" lemma="Aiiba sodo">aiiba samabiyo</char>. Godehe gili osolalosine, gili aiisia auba samabiyo. Eesenaga, eemale. Auyalesenaga, aumabiyo. Sulu auba saeyo, amo isolu dobu.<verse eid="JAS 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="s">Isolu galagololu inolohe Godedai sulu sodo amomo, kiwida</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 5:13" />Gili aleba ugi, inolo uleno higinilu sefia elenaga, amo gahe Godedai sulu saamale. Uleno henefia elenaga, amo gahe Godene wi digisia, gasa saamale. <verse eid="JAS 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 5:14" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.14 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="MRK 6:13">Mag 6.13</ref></char></note>Gili aleba ugi, inolo uleno walefasenaga, amo ehe <char style="w" lemma="Sese">sesene</char> guni inolo noolo e labea milesi weyo dobu. Aufia, ilihe Godedai sulu selesia, Saminilone wi saabia alefasia, walea hano e domalafea sagaeyo dobu. <verse eid="JAS 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 5:15" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.15 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="MAT 17:18-20">Mad 17.18-20</ref></char></note>Aufia, ilihe <char style="w" lemma="Asigi ule ufulu">asigi ule ufia</char> ligia, Godedai sulu selesenaga, Saminilohe walefa inolo amo waiba ofelesi, e degeyobafe. Ausi, ehe <char style="w" lemma="Wolu / Wolu mololo">wolu</char> noolo mololunaga, amo Saminilohe wolu amo galiyobafe. <verse eid="JAS 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 5:16" />Aulugulu, Godehe gili waiba homesine, gili koleba, gine geleba fogaba saafia, gili gine geleba hilisesia, <char style="w" lemma="Godedai sulu selefe">Godedai sulu saaba</char> homale. <char style="w">Isolu galagololu</char> inolohe Godedai sulu sodo mana amohe, kiwida ligia, dabalu mololo. <verse eid="JAS 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 5:17" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.17 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="1KI 17:1">1Kin 17.1</ref>; <ref loc="1KI 18:1">18.1</ref></char></note>Elaiya e-mo, inolo nini labe yagulu. Aufia, ehe Godedai kiwigaaba sulu selesia, hele sugamabiyoba selesi, Isolaele helea ami hele sugabale ligia, hamu osoloafia, aube kaabeba alolu. <verse eid="JAS 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 5:18" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5.18 </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="1KI 18:42-45">1Kin 18.42-45</ref></char></note>Aufia, ehe Godedai sulu saabia selesi, anakiwihe helefealufea hele mesi, edo gelumo haiba soboba yaalu.<verse eid="JAS 5:18" /></para>
  <para style="s">Inolo eno afasia daalu labemo, nini e lubia obegeyo dobu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19-20" style="v" sid="JAS 5:19-20" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">5.19-20 </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="PRO 10:12">Snd 10.12</ref>; <ref loc="GAL 6:1">Gal 6.1</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 4:8">1Fid 4.8</ref></char>
    </note>Ne nelewodali, ne nanodali, doma. Gili ulenohe sulu seale sodomo afasia, dedaleba labihe, elewo nohe e haiba lubia obegesenaga, amo eweguba hilisemale. Inolo ulenohe, wolu mololo inolo no, heleba daaba labe amone lubia obegefe amo, e olalofealo sugabu amone, siba dafelefe. Mana amofea alefasia, Godehe wolu saludialemo hamasia heesia galiyobafe.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JAS 5:19-20">
    <figure style="fig" alt="End of book bilas" file="EndOfBookOnobasulu_Epistles.tiff" size="span" loc="End of Book" ref="5.19-20" /><verse eid="JAS 5:19-20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 5" />
</usx>